%N A086260 Number of symmetric n X n conference matrices.
%D A086260 Symmetric conference matrices are in bijection with labeled conference two-graphs. Thus, a(n) = 2^{n-1} * Sum_C (n! / |Aut(C)|), where C runs over unlabeled conference two-graphs. A catalog of conference two-graphs which includes their automorphism orders is given by Spence and is complete for n < 38 [Spence, 1995]. - _Andrei Zabolotskii_, Aug 23 2026
%H A086260 Edward Spence, <a href="https://www.maths.gla.ac.uk/~es/twograph/conf2Graph.php">Conference Two-Graphs</a>.
%H A086260 Edward Spence, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/0024-3795(95)00158-N">Regular two-graphs on 36 vertices</a>, Linear Algebra and its Applications, 226-228 (1995), 459-497.
%H A086260 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/C-Matrix.html">C-Matrix</a>
%e A086260 For n = 18, the only conference matrix M up to signed permutations is the Paley matrix. The automorphism group order of M and the corresponding conference two-graph C is |Aut(C)| = |PSigmaL_2(17)| = |PSL_2(17)| = A352806(11) = 2448.
%Y A086260 Cf. A086261, A086262, A000952.
